Subject: Exploded Cantor Supervised Mock Loop Activation

@ [source] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-07-30_cantor_supervised_mock_loop_activation\Dictated_Cantor_Supervised_Mock_Loop_Activation_Source.sop
@ [manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-07-30_cantor_supervised_mock_loop_activation\Source_Document_Manifest.sop
@ [runtime_formation] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Codex_Supervised_Ecosystem_Runtime.sop
@ [role_boundary] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Shaliach_Role_Delineation.sop
@ [core_proof] C:\Project\Cantor\proofs\CEB_Deterministic_Baseline_Release_Audit.sop
@ [lifecycle_proof] C:\Project\Cantor\proofs\Cantor_Supervised_Local_Lifecycle_Proof.sop

& [InputSubject] is continued in-scope Cantor implementation after the signed runtime formation's prerequisite gate passed
  + [source_intention] is continue productive Cantor work for the requested four-hour shift
  + [existing_frontier] is ImplementationProgression phase_1_mock_loop
  + [activation_question] is what smallest implementation proves the supervised ecosystem protocol without importing live Codex or effect authority

& [DelineatedBoundary] is deterministic protocol proof only
  + [inside] is one commission, one frame, one work packet, one mock Codex query, one Cantor return, one candidate, one Observer review, one final decision, and one inspectable transcript
  + [outside] is live Codex app-server or SDK control, process supervision, remote or destructive effects, Git mutation, provider inference, notifications, sessions, persistence, multi-worker scheduling, promotion, and compiled faculty programs
  + [reference] is the existing read-only cantor_core protocol used by the Cantor mock participant
  + [uncertainty] is the later live-control transport and persistent manager-process boundary

& [ConstraintLedger] is source-grounded
  + [source_preservation] is the user continuation statement remains separate and unmodified
  + [prior_formation] is phase_1 must precede every later supervised-runtime phase
  + [least_authority] is semantic validation does not authorize an effect
  + [single_authority] is one admitted cantor_core protocol response remains semantic proof
  + [determinism] is identities, logical time, order, and adapter outputs are fixture-controlled
  + [correlation] is every non-root message has one existing causal predecessor in the same correlation
  + [addressing] is consumers accept only messages addressed to their exact identity
  + [replay] is message and idempotency identities cannot be accepted twice
  + [progress] is each transition advances the bounded lifecycle or returns a fault
  + [immutability] is the completed transcript is returned as review evidence and is not edited in place

& [ConceptualDataModel] is the essential semantic substrate
  + [CommissionContract] is principal, purpose, requested result, authority grant, required review checks, budgets, evidence obligation, proof obligation, activation tick, expiry tick, and lifecycle state
  + [AuthorityGrant] is projects, semantic operations, tools, data scopes, and effect classes
  + [WorkPacket] is exact worker, subject, purpose, requested result, acceptance criteria, authority subset, frame digest, and budget subset
  + [ParticipantAddress] is principal, manager, Codex thread, Cantor participant, Observer, or EffectBroker with stable identity
  + [EcosystemMessageEnvelope] is profile, identity, causation, correlation, sender, recipient, kind, subject, frame, authority, typed payload, proof references, response expectation, idempotency identity, and logical tick
  + [MessageTranscript] is the append-only ordered accepted envelope set plus seen identity, idempotency, and semantic-cycle indexes
  + [CandidateArtifact] is candidate identity, immutable content digest, summary, satisfied-criterion claims, proof references, and requested effects
  + [ReviewDecision] is disposition, check results, reasons, candidate identity, and final progress state
  + [CycleOutcome] is commission, work packet, Cantor response, candidate, review, final decision, transcript, and metrics
  + [EcosystemFault] is code, stage, message, and related identities

& [LogicalModel] is a guarded state-transition graph
  + [transition] is commissioned to framed
  + [transition] is framed to assigned
  + [transition] is assigned to Cantor_query_requested
  + [transition] is Cantor_query_requested to Cantor_returned
  + [transition] is Cantor_returned to candidate_returned
  + [transition] is candidate_returned to reviewed
  + [transition] is reviewed to accepted, revise, yield, stop, or fault
  + [invalid_transition] returns EcosystemFault without appending a successor
  + [logical_tick] replaces wall-clock time for deterministic expiry and deadline proof

& [MessageAdmissionDepthContract] is the local trust gate
  + [activation] is before any message changes transcript or lifecycle state
  + [actor] is the MessageTranscript admission boundary
  + [data] is envelope, commission, work packet, current frame, seen indexes, and current logical tick
  + [policy] is exact profile, kind-to-payload, address, frame, authority subset, correlation, causation, deadline, budget, message identity, idempotency, and cycle validation
  + [proof] is accepted transcript order or a typed fault with no partial append
  + [failure] is invalid profile, wrong recipient, stale frame, authority denial, broken causation, correlation mismatch, replay, cycle, expiry, unexpected kind, or budget exhaustion
  @ [weave] supports CSR-RT-005 and CSR-RT-007
  @ [weave] constrains ApprovalAndEffectBoundary

& [MockCodexDepthContract] is deterministic two-step worker behavior
  + [activation] is one accepted assignment then one accepted Cantor return
  + [actor] is one exact Codex thread address
  + [data] is fixture-owned protocol request and candidate artifact
  + [service] is emit one Cantor query after assignment and one candidate after Cantor return
  + [policy] is no repository access, model inference, tool discovery, effects, or hidden state
  + [proof] is exact repeatable envelopes and adapter call counts
  + [failure] is wrong message kind, wrong recipient, repeated call, or non-success Cantor response
  @ [weave] implements ImplementationProgression phase_1_mock_loop only

& [CantorParticipantDepthContract] is existing-core delegation
  + [activation] is one admitted Cantor query addressed to one exact participant
  + [actor] is one purpose-scoped deterministic participant adapter
  + [data] is ProtocolRequest and ProtocolResponse
  + [service] is execute through a caller-supplied exact cantor_core protocol function or fixture adapter
  + [policy] is no independent semantic logic and no broader requested authority
  + [proof] is the returned cantor_core ProtocolResponse and proof fields
  + [failure] is protocol fault, request mismatch, or adapter error
  @ [weave] supports CSR-RT-002 and CSR-RT-004

& [ObserverReviewDepthContract] is deterministic acceptance review
  + [activation] is after one candidate and one successful Cantor response exist
  + [actor] is one exact Observer address
  + [data] is commission, work packet, candidate, Cantor response, and transcript
  + [policy] is require all acceptance criteria claimed, required proof references present, successful Cantor response, zero requested effects, and preserved authority
  + [proof] is named honesty, security, protocol, criteria, and effect-boundary check results
  + [failure] is revise, yield, stop, or fault rather than implicit acceptance
  @ [weave] supports SupervisedBuildCycle steps 7 and 8 without claiming model-based faculty execution

& [BudgetAndCycleDepthContract] is bounded continuation
  + [activation] is every proposed append and adapter transition
  + [data] is maximum messages, maximum call depth, maximum logical ticks, maximum serialized bytes, and semantic fingerprints
  + [policy] is fail before limit violation and reject repeated equivalent subject-frame-kind-payload state
  + [proof] is final metrics and typed limit fault fixtures
  @ [weave] implements DuplexReentrancyControl for the Phase 1 single-cycle profile

& [AcceptanceSet] is implementation-ready
  + [SML-001] is strict serializable CommissionContract, AuthorityGrant, WorkPacket, participant, envelope, payload, candidate, review, outcome, and fault machine forms
  + [SML-002] is authority intersection rejects a work packet or message broader than the commission
  + [SML-003] is exact addressing, frame, correlation, and causation validation before transcript append
  + [SML-004] is message identity, idempotency, and semantic-cycle replay defense
  + [SML-005] is deterministic logical expiry, message, byte, and call-depth budgets
  + [SML-006] is one two-step mock Codex adapter and one existing-core Cantor participant adapter
  + [SML-007] is one deterministic Observer review that cannot authorize or perform effects
  + [SML-008] is one successful exact transcript from commission through decision
  + [SML-009] is negative proof for wrong recipient, stale frame, broken causation, correlation mismatch, authority expansion, replay, expiry, budget, effect request, missing criterion, and adapter fault
  + [SML-010] is deterministic serialization and repeated-run equality
  + [SML-011] is no live Codex, process, provider, persistence, notification, session, promotion, or Git authority

& [PruningTrace] preserves rejected growth
  + [pruned] is live Codex transport because phase_2 requires separate current official-interface research and proof
  + [pruned] is persistent database or service state because Phase 1 only requires an inspectable returned transcript
  + [pruned] is async runtime because the deterministic single-cycle profile has no concurrent wait
  + [pruned] is UUID generation and wall clock because fixture-controlled identities and logical ticks are required for exact replay
  + [pruned] is general-purpose multi-agent orchestration because one manager, one mock worker, one Cantor participant, and one Observer are sufficient
  + [pruned] is external effects because the slice must prove denial before EffectBroker formation
  + [pruned] is neural routing because deterministic protocol correctness remains the oracle

& [SevenFoldTrace] records saturation
  + [fold_1] is continuation intent to Phase 1 boundary
  + [fold_2] is Phase 1 boundary to conceptual records
  + [fold_3] is records to exact transition and admission gates
  + [fold_4] is gates to authority, replay, expiry, budget, and cycle faults
  + [fold_5] is runtime path to mock adapter and existing-core seams
  + [fold_6] is candidate return to deterministic Observer acceptance and effect denial
  + [fold_7] is implementation shape to proof matrix and later-phase locks
  + [exhaustion_state] is phase_locked_for_effect_free_deterministic_mock_loop
  + [growth_seed_set] is read-only live Codex adapter research, durable transcript persistence, streamed event translation, approval forwarding, and process-hosted manager runtime
